stances needed by the body from food?","hi":"खाद्य पदार्थों से शरीर को मिलने वाले आवश्यक तत्त्व क्या कहलाते हैं?","ans":"Nutrients","ans_hi":"पोषक तत्त्व","options":[{"en":"Waste substances","hi":"अपशिष्ट पदार्थ"},{"en":"Germs","hi":"कीटाणु"},{"en":"Nutrients","hi":"पोषक तत्त्व"},{"en":"Dust","hi":"धूल"}],"correct":2,"kind":"core","topic":"Core GK / मूल ज्ञान","marks":1,"_domain":"CURATED_ANSWER"},{"en":"Which organ pumps blood through the body?","hi":"शरीर में रक्त पंप करने वाला अंग कौन-सा है?","ans":"Heart","ans_hi":"हृदय","options":[{"en":"Small intestine","hi":"छोटी आँत"},{"en":"Pancreas","hi":"अग्न्याशय"},{"en":"Heart","hi":"हृदय"},{"en":"Stomach","hi":"आमाशय"}],"correct":2,"kind":"core","topic":"Core GK / मूल ज्ञान","marks":1,"_domain":"organs"},{"en":"Which organs help us breathe?","hi":"साँस लेने में कौन-से अंग मदद करते हैं?","ans":"Lungs","ans_hi":"फेफड़े","options":[{"en":"Kidneys","hi":"गुर्दे"},{"en":"Lungs","hi":"फेफड़े"},{"en":"Skull","hi":"खोपड़ी"},{"en":"Heart","hi":"हृदय"}],"correct":1,"kind":"core","topic":"Core GK / मूल ज्ञान","marks":1,"_domain":"organs"},{"en":"Which organ controls thinking and body movements?","hi":"सोच और शारीरिक गतिविधियों को नियंत्रित कौन-सा अंग करता है?","ans":"Brain","ans_hi":"मस्तिष्क","options":[{"en":"Liver","hi":"यकृत"},{"en":"Gallbladder","hi":"पित्ताशय"},{"en":"Brain","hi":"मस्तिष्क"},{"en":"Pancreas","hi":"अग्न्याशय"}],"correct":2,"kind":"core","topic":"Core GK / मूल ज्ञान","marks":1,"_domain":"organs"},{"en":"What is the hardest substance in the human body?","hi":"मानव शरीर का सबसे कठोर पदार्थ कौन-सा है?","ans":"Tooth enamel","ans_hi":"दाँतों का इनेमल","options":[{"en":"Cartilage","hi":"उपास्थि"},{"en":"Skin","hi":"त्वचा"},{"en":"Hair","hi":"बाल"},{"en":"Tooth enamel","hi":"दाँतों का इनेमल"}],"correct":3,"kind":"core","topic":"Core GK / मूल ज्ञान","marks":1,"_domain":"CURATED_ANSWER"},{"en":"Which sense organ is linked to taste?","hi":"स्वाद का अनुभव किस इंद्रिय से होता है?","ans":"Tongue","ans_hi":"जीभ","options":